[{"id":"VRCE-3-27-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":1,"english":"Seeing Düşaņa slain in fight along with Trisiră, Khara, witnessing Rāma's prowess, was filled with fear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.97,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1fcfc35a685e26d47c6484b5067e506eb2f9428a61b88cab3c51e812244f94c8","compact":"c1fee06650f4ffea18769490fa2f906f3891c03b9d0f119ef392af6a3f5a1989","nasal":"c1fee06650f4ffea18769490fa2f906f3891c03b9d0f119ef392af6a3f5a1989"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":2,"english":"Seeing that irresistible Raksasa host-even Düşaņa and Triſirā-slain by the mighty Rāma alone, and seeing the great courage that was made in the army, that Raksasa, Khara, was seized with despondency. Then as Namuci advances against Väsava, Khara stretching his powerful bow, advanced against Răma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e5c478f8848621cf9f790c102986eb523b8714581019489d6bb05c03796655d","compact":"1efc1ef01097e39bf06cc568684d5f202f7d4deeb78ef76d6f74460db0ee67fb","nasal":"1efc1ef01097e39bf06cc568684d5f202f7d4deeb78ef76d6f74460db0ee67fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":3,"english":"Seeing that irresistible Raksasa host-even Düşaņa and Triſirā-slain by the mighty Rāma alone, and seeing the great courage that was made in the army, that Raksasa, Khara, was seized with despondency. Then as Namuci advances against Väsava, Khara stretching his powerful bow, advanced against Răma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.948,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e8af485c7deda27c03b3e5d34d0f2d22374f188373b62592cc8930eacfb8553","compact":"0ff25661966a7662172677402ac4febd188ead4738fd4055afb25169048ac40e","nasal":"0ff25661966a7662172677402ac4febd188ead4738fd4055afb25169048ac40e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":4,"english":"Khara hurled at Rāma nārācas revelling in blood, resembling infuriated venomous snakes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ebaad5c691045c557aa0b90dda7e071d616d7d5409cf48d1873198df65b15007","compact":"c3b382a0e14279c463ff7e7f674d37a9036b21f93ae1216b6accfc04fa853d19","nasal":"c3b382a0e14279c463ff7e7f674d37a9036b21f93ae1216b6accfc04fa853d19"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":5,"english":"Repeatedly twanging his twanging his bow, Khara, mounted on his car, began to range the field, displaying his weapons through his acquired skill.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d391e70b9db0539cce0517f57e75742553398ac82c9087716461923b14ede16","compact":"8440b99b3d03a18f1913d39a33020cd39fb1170dd177e3f3e8a3951b87e8c58a","nasal":"8440b99b3d03a18f1913d39a33020cd39fb1170dd177e3f3e8a3951b87e8c58a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":6,"english":"And that mighty car-warrior covered all sides with his shafts. And secing this, Rāma of a tremendous bow with shafts incapable of being borne, and resembling tongues of flaming fire, entirely enveloped the welkin, even as a cloud pour down showers.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"877c9a2a09e93fca9d167bf9ff3824b37daa9d52cef9d6b1c684f566b7fe37a7","compact":"5ec1a4a6601efc7982830563b205acfaa6c03921feb9ff414522eca710a78e2e","nasal":"5ec1a4a6601efc7982830563b205acfaa6c03921feb9ff414522eca710a78e2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":7,"english":"And that mighty car-warrior covered all sides with his shafts. And secing this, Rāma of a tremendous bow with shafts incapable of being borne, and resembling tongues of flaming fire, entirely enveloped the welkin, even as a cloud pour down showers.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6df9bce02846d90ff01adefa629cffbde5d632f4209f3d5694b1845f2b0011e3","compact":"ca65081006c267b06fd6ffb21457a6ef7dc4ef89cd1be5dd548343e7423cd82c","nasal":"2e844ee308099d218d986d96b64020750a4b5e1bb142138dba30bcdc0db81b8e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":8,"english":"With the sharpened shafts shot by Khara and Rāma, the entire firmament on all sides was thronged.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc47e7a68b628c13da07c58189fd8a88c25505e48e884d97c022d599170c90f3","compact":"0fe3ee4f5580ef9f20f383b84bac967a5090461af8acb47955d613c67d31d04e","nasal":"0fe3ee4f5580ef9f20f383b84bac967a5090461af8acb47955d613c67d31d04e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":9,"english":"And as each enraged was engaged in coping with the other, the sun, enveloped in a net-work of shafts, did not appear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cf358b7b44e2e51631c84cf46673c80aa3f8613662e19aa3fde5ac80eadd742e","compact":"d4daae86e2c61681b62e09b0d677c3ab32592169ca7e3da40aa4dad1f759c95a","nasal":"64a3f79e853fd2f0de4fab2bd2d451ade9b452830064fba04a38da6c5bda52f0"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":10,"english":"As a mighty elephant is struck with the goad, Rāma in the conflict attacked (his opponent) with nalikas and nārācas and sharp-pointed vikarna.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"44fb45340d15d7a77d8c43663bfc9525bd7ef59e20e07318674222428df99859","compact":"46a5557457e4df13729c1ac71c29ebd2eca24021547c0a9b42a1e209d83d7c2a","nasal":"46a5557457e4df13729c1ac71c29ebd2eca24021547c0a9b42a1e209d83d7c2a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":11,"english":"And as that Rākşasa sat on his car, bow in hand, all creatures saw him, as if he were the very destroyer with the noose in his hand.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f802ccbe10b94cff1570c66a7434df4cc020c3f14148356783703fd0c1c684a0","compact":"5aa95ab35a530db7f234306e28a57f9b1570ce1952684642bdff3006d1101240","nasal":"bbb09d979e8c0a100e0ad8e24db65a08b21c8d65ed53fd665b047c9832724c1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":12,"english":"Seeing that one powerful like the lion, and gifted with the vigorous gait of the lion, Rāma was not moved, as a lion seeing a puny deer (is not moved).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"48e73fa09767ea5c414d471e231031d6afadef3f078f5223142098ba9558db09","compact":"84112c35423b5f96a8f0cd47178ac711d8badae4aaa24fae7e55166605de7492","nasal":"f0df97d9ecdb2c10ebea94fa2ffabc0ecc5162e698147edf45dd1b681bee0dd2"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":13,"english":"And then as an insect falls into a flame, Khara mounting a mighty car, resembling the sun, approached Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.682,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78bd94e88cbc9c622f2f0471150a18afbd217ef21699d093c7a3b633332f1914","compact":"b0b99a0d0b863a91e01a9a96747d06940692a7a2d8756c5f8269e8af939e973b","nasal":"8ed8c9f674e68d3c3784c286f50f19e805b2d81dcb4212b3fcdc70ea7d5e79e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":14,"english":"And, displaying his lightness of hand, Khara severed the bow of the magnanimous Rāma, with the arrow (fixed on it) at the place where it is grasped.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b7031afcd119915f2032d3c526657d221b18ec1264b024e8e08d1fb72019c6b7","compact":"11cf5c9b7849bfdadd69178a4640357df1c44642ee917e703e7dc0410613e193","nasal":"11cf5c9b7849bfdadd69178a4640357df1c44642ee917e703e7dc0410613e193"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":15,"english":"Then taking up seven other shafts, resplendent like the thunderbolt of Sakra, Khara, enraged, sent them into (Rāma's) main-joints, and then afflicting Rāma of unparalleled energy with a thousand shafts, Khara sent up in that conflict a loud shout.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af59f7a6785ee86a020ae68269ee3999f79260726f08743458cdd252bb373652","compact":"ca8e49241351025c30a1aa8d96dca90020537de7e1a4d933415bf77b76bc0299","nasal":"ca8e49241351025c30a1aa8d96dca90020537de7e1a4d933415bf77b76bc0299"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":16,"english":"And riven by the shafts discharged by Khara, Rāma's mail resembling the sun fell to the ground.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.983,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0dc8570471771e0e432341243c68ea3c5a5964da6c541eab4edbf4e8eae1803a","compact":"7424b98536a6849fd3c99a6ae0922b63f5b3cde06ea8701c6d56c290461de6b4","nasal":"7424b98536a6849fd3c99a6ae0922b63f5b3cde06ea8701c6d56c290461de6b4"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":17,"english":"And pierced with those arrow, all over his body, and inflamed with rage, Rāghava appeared in the field, like a smokeless flaming fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d681d8957a11f77794d21e9573d4ee6c94e17861ae4ea86379ff199510598469","compact":"8e95d83f080f44d63ee17b5e3fd53fa1371d44301bb2e4d0002e0e919ea15401","nasal":"8e95d83f080f44d63ee17b5e3fd53fa1371d44301bb2e4d0002e0e919ea15401"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":18,"english":"Then that destroyer of foes, Rāma, for compassing the end of his enemy, stringed another mighty bow, sending forth solemn sounds, the redoubtable Vaisnava bow that had been conferred on him by the Maharşi.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"130e663ed0153b937eea43cc7bb5c87fa302d3e2401928eb959b09d55b77b5c8","compact":"5cfc2d669c3f4a31f753998ea92081b952a4f73a4295235c4befac8cccc123f0","nasal":"ed4217ca4f4f0c270b64f3d5d53bd886232fecd9bac0367a1caf655c76d73e49"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":19,"english":"Then that destroyer of foes, Rāma, for compassing the end of his enemy, stringed another mighty bow, sending forth solemn sounds, the redoubtable Vaisnava bow that had been conferred on him by the Maharşi.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cfd315e0a26ce95e38452ec7303276b6570927250a6d6ff22d638606a5e2d34f","compact":"03c90124b0b11352b1f0c3c2a6a614be43c7b9923ff8a009064c3b8327600bc8","nasal":"03c90124b0b11352b1f0c3c2a6a614be43c7b9923ff8a009064c3b8327600bc8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":20,"english":"And uplifting that superior bow, Rāma rushed against Khara. Then with shafts having bent knots and golden feathers, Rāma, wrought up with rage, severed in battle Khara's standard.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d80f08cf457fea50bc863a5de29ede1c0657281acbb0f0fcf7f8f075f7dfffa4","compact":"74587c1d69750731cdd6a2c03e992d232659690fc225875a6bdf9fbd564cea8f","nasal":"5cb6084b3009d3438f4d28c9785da71322fa8f5a1d7c5de0d8faae03fdf25196"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":21,"english":"And on that exceedingly graceful golden standard being hewn down it seemed as if the sun dropped to the earth at the behest of the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e2e653f7bdbfbb3e719dfdf458707b355b21063d6ec877ebe54072dd9c20cac","compact":"cfc4b27cd0b4d9196c02da257a4e153b69dbe35d6475461e9526a2897e2bbd07","nasal":"766589d217176760e15eb4c7985df14f674c0534800e34f0dfa52b8094f147d6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":22,"english":"And thereat Khara, understanding the import of things, fired with wrath, pierced Rāma's breast with five arrows, like one striking an elephant with a goad.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.706,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fi