kritLocator":"3027025","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6274e1a05acf9ab2d2abf9ad78302ad8a648b8bf8642ed178477bc64be2bb026","compact":"5ab6a4ebd849aae236a03fd938f98cc23730f9a0baef1b015aa17baaeee70edf","nasal":"3e40b24e55fa2e51f7e1e93126f2e5baa24e5f186eb5e0a010dffb881a1d1acd"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-26","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":26,"english":"Then that highly energetic one, influenced by anger, assailed the Räkşasa with thirteen närācas whetted on stone and with one that exceedingly powerful one, cut the yoke of the car, with four the four steeds, with the sixth the head of Khara's charioteer, with three the stout trivenu of the car, with two the wheel, and with the twelfth, severing as if in sport Khara's bow with his hand*, with the thirteenth, resembling the thunder-bolt pierced Khara in the encounter. Another text reads: with the arrow set.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-28-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3027026","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"431b512cd9e390607546eae146ee5aed4c5f3834d32f476049f638e2fece9542","compact":"e81f3f961c229ad13089e1d3be7ed3c1bf405e9e3fcce26da89714e84040ef55","nasal":"e81f3f961c229ad13089e1d3be7ed3c1bf405e9e3fcce26da89714e84040ef55"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-27-27","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":27,"verse":27,"english":"Then that highly energetic one, influenced by anger, assailed the Räkşasa with thirteen närācas whetted on stone and with one that exceedingly powerful one, cut the yoke of the car, with four the four steeds, with the sixth the head of Khara's charioteer, with three the stout trivenu of the car, with two the wheel, and with the twelfth, severing as if in sport Khara's bow with his hand*, with the thirteenth, resembling the thunder-bolt pierced Khara in the encounter. Another text read